Run this example in a fresh database:
```sql
CREATE TABLE demo_collection (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
  name TEXT,
  count INTEGER
);
INSERT INTO demo_collection (id, name, count)
VALUES (1, 'Stones', 6), (2, 'Tickets', 2);
UPDATE demo_collection
SET count = count + 1
WHERE id = 1;
DELETE FROM demo_collection
WHERE id = 2;
SELECT name, count
FROM demo_collection;
```
One row remains: `Stones` with a count of `7`.
